1. The Broken HTML File ("Before")

Here is the faulty code containing missing tags, incorrect nesting, and a missing attribute [cite: 9]:
html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Broken Webpage</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Welcome to My Website
    
    <div>
        <p>This paragraph has an <strong>incorrectly nested tag <em>bold and italic text</strong> properly closed?</em></p>
    </div>

    <div>
        <!-- Missing the required href attribute -->
        <a>Click here to visit Google</a>
    </div>

</body>
</html>


2. Identified Errors

When analyzing this code via browser DevTools or an HTML validator, three major issues stand out [cite: 9]:
• Missing Closing Tag: The main heading <h1> is never closed, causing subsequent elements to accidentally inherit header properties in some browsers [cite: 9].
• Incorrect Nesting: Inside the first <div>, the tags overlap incorrectly (<strong><em>...</strong></em>) [cite: 9]. The <em> tag must be closed before the <strong> tag closes [cite: 9].
• Missing Attribute: The anchor <a> tag is missing its vital href attribute, making it an unclickable text element instead of a working link [cite: 9].

3. The Corrected HTML File ("After")

Here is the clean, validated, and properly indented code with all elements fixed [cite: 9]:
html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Fixed Webpage</title>
</head>
<body>

    <!-- Fixed: Added missing closing h1 tag -->
    <h1>Welcome to My Website</h1>
    
    <div>
        <!-- Fixed: Corrected nesting order for strong and em tags -->
        <p>This paragraph has a <strong>properly nested <em>bold and italic text</em> block</strong> now.</p>
    </div>

    <div>
        <!-- Fixed: Added missing href attribute -->
        <a href="https://google.com">Click here to visit Google</a>
    </div>

</body>
</html>



